# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_durable_inbox.py" "DURABLE INBOX GATE: PASS" "durable inbox" "durable webhook inbox (persist-before-202 durability boundary: a delivery persisted then CRASHED before finish is RECOVERED + replayed IDEMPOTENTLY [done:2, payload cleared to {}]; recovery re-submits stale 'processing' + 'queued' but leaves a freshly-locked 'processing' alone; cross-tenant authority — a BUYER tenant role is REFUSED EXECUTE on every *_with_authority fn AND direct table access [42501], so it can never claim/finish/release/recover another tenant's row; the _latest_push residual is CLOSED — a register_push=False recovered stale push does NOT regress newest-push tracking nor mask a newer live push as 'skip'; the persisted payload is content-free. HARDENING [audit P1]: the DURABLE retry budget has its OWN larger ceiling than the in-memory transient-retry budget [floored above it] so a restart-spanning recovery cycle does NOT prematurely dead-letter; a POISON 'failed' row is NOT silently lost — it is VISIBLE in depth(), ALERTED by the watchdog [evaluate_delivery_depth fires delivery_dead_letter on failed>0 + delivery_backlog on a non-draining 'queued' pile, wired end-to-end via watchdog_tick(store=...)], and RE-ARMED by the DLQ sweep [aged 'failed' rows requeued for one fresh budget, a just-failed row left alone by the age gate]; an AGE-BASED reaper drops terminal done/failed rows past the window while KEEPING live 'queued'/'processing' rows)" "durable inbox / 202-then-async DURABILITY (a crash/deploy after the 202 must NOT lose the event; recovery replays exactly once; cross-tenant rows are unreachable; a poison row is surfaced/alerted/re-armed not lost; the watchdog sees the durable depth; terminal rows are reaped by age; RELIABILITY-critical)" 30
